{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"aimless-pearly-squamata","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\n\nThe MCP endpoint's `401` challenge advertises a protected-resource metadata URL that does not\nexist at the edge.\n\n    www-authenticate: Bearer error=\"invalid_token\", ...\n      resource_metadata=\"https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp\"\n\n    GET https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp -> 404\n\n## Scope\n\nRFC 9728 metadata discovery is how an OAuth-capable client learns where to authenticate. A client\nthat follows the advertised URL gets a 404 and cannot discover the resource server.\n\nToday's clients use STATIC bearer PATs and do not consult it, so nothing is currently broken in\npractice — which is why this is P3 rather than higher. It matters if/when OAuth clients are\nenabled, and an advertised-but-missing URL is misleading regardless.\n\n## Pre-existing, not caused by the HTTPS-downgrade fix\n\nConfirmed against the pre-change backup of `/etc/nginx/conf.d/rebar.conf`: there is no such\nlocation block BEFORE or AFTER that deploy. The nginx config has never served the path.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Either the edge serves the advertised metadata document, or the `401` stops advertising a\n      URL that does not resolve.\n- [ ] A check fails if the advertised `resource_metadata` URL is not fetchable.","id":"71fe-2579-28cc-409c","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["mcp","auth","oauth","nginx"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP 401 advertises /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp, which returns 404"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787868673036616001,"uuid":"4e46ecd1-f67a-44ab-902f-c1dfe6a75b90"}